From: IS27 Buddy 1 <is27@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 16:08:18 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Barcode: GUI-set letter map, noise filter, sensor diagnostics

- GUI "Barcode map" box (e.g. A=L B=R C=U D=S) publishes robot/map
  (QoS 1, retained); the car confirms the map in use on robot/tlm/map
  every 5 s. Unmapped letters drive straight; built-in default is all
  straight. START works with or without a map.
- barcode.c: 10 ms debounce on the sensor's D0 (comparator chatter gave
  300-600 changes/s), end-of-barcode wait raised to 0.8 s, console
  diagnostics (per-change log, per-second counts, reasons for rejects).
- comms_frames / codec: map and map-ack frames, covered by
  testing/comms_test (C packer vs Python decoder).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0146ZJZmHJ22aECQtBcDQi4o
